        {
          "id": "SP_BRIAREUM_HAMRUM",
          "name": "Briareum hamrum",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Briareum",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Calyx with straight spindles containing small tubercles arranged in transverse rows and flattened spindles (Figure 8 A). Cortex with straight or bent spindles with complex tubercles (Figure 8 B). Coenenchymal sclerites 0.10 - 0.35 mm long. Medulla additionally has branched sclerites with simple or complex tubercles (Figure 8 C). These sclerites are slightly shorter, up to 0.30 mm long. Sclerites of the surface layer are colourless; interior sclerites are magenta.",
